# Your own ArkaWM shortcuts. Copy this file to ~/.config/arkawm/shortcuts and edit it.
# One shortcut per line: keys = command. A saved change works on the next key press.
#
# Keys: Super (the Windows key), Ctrl, Alt, Shift, joined with +, then one key by its xkb
# name: a letter, a digit, Return, space, F1..F12, Print, slash, ... A letter needs Super,
# Ctrl or Alt, so it can still be typed. A shortcut here wins over ArkaWM's own on the same keys.
#
# ArkaWM's own shortcuts:
#   Super+L lock          Super+S search apps     Super+Enter / Ctrl+Alt+T terminal
#   Super+E files         Super+I settings        Ctrl+Shift+Esc system monitor
#   Super+D desktop       Super+V clipboard       Super+A quick settings   Super+N notifications
#   Super+Left/Right snap Super+Up maximise       Super+Down restore or minimise
#   Alt+Tab switch window Alt+F4 close            Print screenshot   Shift+Print / Super+Shift+S part
#   Super+Alt+C format wheel   Super+Alt+E edit wheel   Alt+Shift+E end the session
#
# Examples (remove the # to use one):
# Super+B = firefox
# Super+K = kate
# Ctrl+Alt+N = kate ~/notes.txt
